From: Patrik Eriksson <patrik.m.eriksson@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:23:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] web: APERTAR_WEB_PREVIEW_RECORDING_FPS caps or pauses the
 web preview while a raw take runs

Why: when a browser shows the live preview, captureWebPreviewFrame downsamples the 1280x720
preview to 640x360 on libcamera's completion thread, inside the serial per-frame cycle, for
every frame at up to 30 fps. The kb's research (working/dng-chain, R5, R7, S2) names it the one
per-frame image pass left on that thread and the first candidate for the frames lost at capture
in short takes with the WebUI open (hardware-log 2026-10-31); the 10-minute takes that stayed
clean ran with the WebUI closed.

What: a lock-free CameraController::rawTakeActive() (the write queue's gauge flag) tells the
completion thread that a take runs; the web preview is then rate-limited to
APERTAR_WEB_PREVIEW_RECORDING_FPS (default 30, unchanged; 0 = no web preview frames while
recording). README row.

Tested: both files syntax-check (CameraController.cpp with the libcamera block on, no new
errors). Not run on the Pi: the two-take test (60 s with the WebUI closed, then open) decides
whether the knob is needed, and =0 or =10 is the fix if it is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
